NEW["fig-dm-write"] = (None, None,
 "A layer can change the stream only as much as its write is large compared with the stream. " + TEN_EN + " It plots, for each layer, the RMS of the attention and MLP outputs divided by the RMS of the state each one read, averaged over tokens. A few outlier tokens lift some layers far above the typical token; the per-token median is up to 64 times lower at layer 47 of the ordinary Hyper-Connections model and 34 times lower at layer 41 of the separate-heads mHC model. It tests how far each design lets late layers move the stream, and whether separate heads shrink or grow the writes. The ordinary AttnRes (Full) model writes two outsized sources. The MLP of layer 44 writes 1,339 times the RMS of what it read, and that of layer 47 about 1,006 times; its separate-heads twin writes nothing of that size. A follow-up shows what the layer-44 source does. Every later read gives it a softmax weight below 1e-5 except layer 45's MLP (0.015), layer 48's attention (0.034) and layer 48's MLP (0.68, on every token), and its size, 53,000 times the median source, turns that 0.68 into 99.8% of what layer 48's MLP reads. Removing it from that one read costs the whole 8.95 nats, and rescaling it to the median size costs as much. Through its size, layer 44 passes its output to layer 48's MLP alone. The layer-47 source costs 0.008 nats.",
 "一层能改变残差流多少，取决于它的写入相对残差流有多大。" + TEN_ZH + "它画出每一层注意力和 MLP 输出的 RMS，除以它们各自读到的状态的 RMS，再对 token 取平均。少数离群 token 会把某些层抬得远高于一般 token：在普通 Hyper-Connections 模型的第 47 层，每个 token 的中位数比平均值低 64 倍；在独立头 mHC 模型的第 41 层低 34 倍。它检验每种结构让后面的层能把残差流移动多远，以及独立头让写入变小还是变大。普通 AttnRes (Full) 模型写出两个超大的来源。第 44 层的 MLP 写出它读到内容 RMS 的 1,339 倍，第 47 层的约 1,006 倍；它的独立头孪生模型没有这么大的写入。一个后续实验显示了第 44 层这个来源的作用。后面的每次读取给它的 softmax 权重都低于 1e-5，只有第 45 层的 MLP（0.015）、第 48 层的注意力（0.034）和第 48 层的 MLP（0.68，每个 token 都是）例外；而它的大小是中位数来源的 53,000 倍，使这 0.68 变成第 48 层 MLP 读到内容的 99.8%。只从这一次读取中去掉它，就要付全部 8.95 nats；把它缩放到中位数大小，代价也一样。第 44 层靠它的大小，只把输出传给第 48 层的 MLP。第 47 层的来源只值 0.008 nats。")
